From: Giovanni Gherdovich <ggherdovich@suse.cz>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 12:38:06 +0200
Subject: kabi: add back field cppc_cpudata::node
Patch-mainline: Never, kabi workaround
References: jsc#PED-16818 bsc#1272555

Backport of upstream commit d80a75624051 ("cpufreq: CPPC: Remove
cpu_data_list") removes field "node" from kabi protected struct
cppc_cpudata. Here we add it back to preserve kabi.

The field in question is a linked list node, so that a list is
threaded through all instances of "struct cppc_cpudata" (one per cpu).
Crucially the list nodes are managed internally by the sole in-tree
user (cppc_cpufreq driver), and no kernel code populates that field
with data for the module to use. Its use is exclusively for the
module's internal bookkeeping.

An external module expecting the "struct list_head node" field where
it was, would be also managing it privately without leak, thus an
appropriate padding would work all the same.

The field takes the space of two pointers and could be replaced with
padding, but that would indicate the space is free to be used for
additional members, while the situation here is slightly different.

We prefer to leave the backport patch unaltered and add back the field
in a kabi-specific fix, as to highlight the kabi impact of the change;
one could also have amended that backport patch as to not touch
struct cppc_cpudata at all.

Signed-off-by: Giovanni Gherdovich <ggherdovich@suse.cz>
Reviewed-by: Petr Pavlu <petr.pavlu@suse.com>
---
 include/acpi/cppc_acpi.h |    1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/include/acpi/cppc_acpi.h
+++ b/include/acpi/cppc_acpi.h
@@ -144,6 +144,7 @@ struct cppc_perf_fb_ctrs {
 
 /* Per CPU container for runtime CPPC management. */
 struct cppc_cpudata {
+	struct list_head node;      /* Field is unused in-tree. Kept in for kABI compatibility. */
 	struct cppc_perf_caps perf_caps;
 	struct cppc_perf_ctrls perf_ctrls;
 	struct cppc_perf_fb_ctrs perf_fb_ctrs;
